## 6.3 Create `README.md`

<WritingBlock id="62841" variant="document"># PyCoin (PYC)

**An Educational Decentralized Cryptocurrency Built with Python**

PyCoin is an educational cryptocurrency project designed to demonstrate the engineering principles behind decentralized digital currencies.

The project implements a native blockchain, cryptographic wallets, digital signatures, transactions, Proof of Work consensus, mining, peer-to-peer networking, and a web-based wallet and blockchain explorer.

## Project Objectives

- Understand blockchain architecture.
- Implement cryptographic transaction verification.
- Develop a native cryptocurrency.
- Build a Proof of Work consensus mechanism.
- Implement decentralized peer-to-peer networking.
- Develop a wallet and blockchain explorer.
- Apply professional software engineering and security practices.

## Technology Stack

| Component | Technology |
|---|---|
| Core language | Python |
| Backend | FastAPI |
| Cryptography | PyNaCl |
| Hashing | SHA-256 |
| Database | SQLite |
| ORM | SQLAlchemy |
| Frontend | React + Vite |
| Styling | CSS / Tailwind CSS (later phase) |
| Testing | Pytest + Vitest |
| Version control | Git + GitHub |

## Project Status

**Current phase:** Phase 0 — Project Initialization

See [documentation/PROJECT_STATUS.md](documentation/PROJECT_STATUS.md).

## Development Setup

### Backend

```bash
git clone YOUR_REPOSITORY_URL
cd pycoin

python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate

python -m pip install -e ".[dev]"

pytest -v
python -m pycoin
```

### Frontend

```bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
```

### API Documentation

When the backend is running:

- API: http://127.0.0.1:8000
- Swagger: http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs
- Health: http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/health

## Development Roadmap

- Phase 0: Project initialization
- Phase 1: Cryptographic foundation
- Phase 2: Blockchain data structures
- Phase 3: Transaction engine
- Phase 4: Cryptocurrency wallet
- Phase 5: Mempool
- Phase 6: Proof of Work mining
- Phase 7: Consensus mechanism
- Phase 8: Blockchain persistence
- Phase 9: Peer-to-peer networking
- Phase 10: Blockchain synchronization
- Phase 11: REST API
- Phase 12: React wallet application
- Phase 13: Blockchain explorer
- Phase 14: Security and testing
- Phase 15: Deployment and documentation

## Security Notice

PyCoin is an educational project. It is not intended for handling real funds or production cryptocurrency transactions.

Do not use experimental wallet implementations with valuable private keys.

## License

MIT License — see LICENSE.
</WritingBlock>

Create `LICENSE` with the standard MIT license text, using your chosen copyright holder and year.

