## 6.5 Create `documentation/ARCHITECTURE.md`

<WritingBlock id="62843" variant="document"># PyCoin — System Architecture

## 1. Overview

PyCoin is an educational decentralized cryptocurrency implemented using Python.

The system follows a modular architecture with independent blockchain, cryptography, wallet, transaction, consensus, networking, storage, and API components.

## 2. Architecture Layers

### Cryptography
- SHA-256 hashing.
- Ed25519 digital signatures.
- Public and private key management.
- Address derivation.

### Blockchain Core
- Block headers.
- Block validation.
- Genesis block.
- Merkle trees.
- Blockchain management.

### Transaction Engine
- Transaction construction.
- Signature verification.
- Account nonce validation.
- Balance validation.
- Transaction fees.

### Consensus
- Proof of Work.
- Mining.
- Difficulty adjustment.
- Chain selection.
- Fork resolution.

### Networking
- Peer discovery.
- Node communication.
- Transaction propagation.
- Block propagation.
- Synchronization.

### Storage
- SQLite.
- SQLAlchemy.
- Alembic migrations.
- Persistent blockchain state.

### API
- FastAPI.
- Request validation.
- Node health.
- Blockchain endpoints.

### Frontend
- React.
- Wallet interface.
- Transaction interface.
- Blockchain explorer.
- Mining dashboard.

## 3. Ledger Model

The initial implementation uses an account-based ledger.

Accounts maintain balances and transaction nonces. Balances are derived from validated ledger transitions.

## 4. Consensus

The educational network will use Proof of Work.

Nodes independently validate blocks and select the valid chain with the greatest accumulated work.

## 5. Security Principles

- Use established cryptographic libraries.
- Never transmit private keys to backend services.
- Use deterministic transaction serialization.
- Prevent replay and double-spending.
- Validate all incoming network messages.
- Protect against denial-of-service attacks.
- Keep development secrets outside version control.

## 6. Deployment Strategy

Development begins with local single-node execution.

Later phases introduce multiple independent nodes, private testnet deployment, containerization, monitoring, and recovery mechanisms.

## 7. Scope

PyCoin is initially an educational cryptocurrency. Its successful implementation does not automatically establish production security or economic viability.
</WritingBlock>

